files that were already fully read.\n\n## Lens\n**Phase 1: The Intent vs. 
Reality Check** - Logic Gaps\n\n## Expected vs. Observed\n| Expected Behavior | 
Observed Risk |\n|---|---|\n| When `lines_read` is "full" (case-insensitive, 
with optional surrounding whitespace), any subsequent read should return `False`
(no need to read) | The method only checks exact match after `.lower()`, so 
"FULL " (with trailing space) is not recognized as "full" |\n| The method should
be robust to minor data formatting variations | Files marked as fully read but 
with whitespace in `lines_read` are unnecessarily re-read |\n| User/agent 
convenience: forgiving of whitespace in stored data | Strict matching causes 
functional bugs |\n\n## Root Cause\nLine 257 in `should_read_file`: `if 
match.lines_read.lower() == "full":`\n- Uses `.lower()` for case-insensitivity 
(good)\n- Does `.strip()` for whitespace (missing!)\n- Result: `"FULL ".lower()`
gives `"full "` which does not equal `"full"`\n\nThis causes the method to 
proceed to `LineRange.from_str()` which fails to parse `"FULL "` as a valid 
range, returning `None`, which then triggers the "invalid lines_read format" 
path, returning `True` (need to read).\n\n## Fix Plan\n1. Change line 257 to: 
`if match.lines_read.strip().lower() == "full":`\n2. Add `.strip()` to remove 
leading/trailing whitespace before comparison\n3. This maintains 
case-insensitivity while being forgiving of whitespace\n\n## Status: FIXED\n\n##
