Perfect! I have successfully completed the task:

## Summary

I identified and fixed **ONE real bug** in the `src/henchman/agents/working_memory.py` file using the **Four Lenses of Failure** methodology and strict TDD:

### The Bug
The `should_read_file` method failed to recognize "full" file reads when the `lines_read` field had surrounding whitespace (e.g., "FULL ", " full", " full "). This caused unnecessary re-reads of files that were already fully read.

### Root Cause
Line 257: `if match.lines_read.lower() == "full":` used `.lower()` for case-insensitivity but didn't use `.strip()` for whitespace removal. So `"FULL ".lower()` gave `"full "` which didn't equal `"full"`.

### The Fix
Changed line 257 to: `if match.lines_read.strip().lower() == "full":`

### TDD Process Followed
1. **Analyzed** the code through all four lenses
2. **Documented** the bug in `.agent_tasks/four-lenses-agents-working_memory/README.md`
3. **Wrote failing test first** (added `test_memory_should_read_file_full_with_whitespace()` to test file)
4. **Implemented minimal fix** (added `.strip()`)
5. **Verified all tests pass** (46 tests, including new one)
6. **Updated documentation** to mark bug as FIXED

### Files Changed
1. `src/henchman/agents/working_memory.py` - Line 257 fix
2. `tests/agents/test_working_memory.py` - Added new test method

The bug was in **core functionality** (file reading optimization logic), not style or documentation. The fix is **minimal and surgical**, addressing exactly one bug without refactoring unrelated code. All tests pass, maintaining 98% coverage for the module.[tech_lead] completed work
